Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790326799999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the 2850 high is a single-bar spike (bar 117) with a 74.39-point upper tail, and bars 118-120 give no follow-through above it; a failed breakout would rotate price back into the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Upside spike attempts inside this window have repeatedly failed: 2557.46 (bar 92), 2680 (bar 107) and 2609.02 (bar 110) were each closed back inside the range, so an overshoot above a range top is a recurring pattern here.", "Bar 119 closes at 2684.16, back below the 2771 prior swing high, so the break above that swing high is not yet accepted.", "Near-term momentum has turned down: bars 118 and 119 are the first two consecutive lower closes since bar 113, and bar 119 closes in the lower quarter of its range.", "Bars 87-113 (27 of the last 34 bars before the breakout) traded two-sided inside 2357.18-2680, so an alternative read is a broad trading range with only a marginal upside overshoot, i.e., phase more channel/range than a fresh spike.", "Bars 115 and 116 barely advance (closes 2632.98 and 2642.90) between the two strong bars, and the leg from bar 106 to 2850 contains overlapping pullbacks, which is channel rather than pure spike behavior."], "evidence_for": ["The 120-bar window shows an unbroken sequence of higher swing lows (1368.42, 1512.91, 1597.72, 1803.74, 2357.18, 2633.31) and higher swing highs (1944.39, 2771, 2850), which is the core of the bull-trend classification.", "Bar 84 is a large bull trend bar closing at the top of its range with follow-through to 2771 (bars 85-86), showing acceptance above the 1803.74-1974.46 range rather than a one-bar overshoot.", "The compressed final range (bars 73-83 inside 1863.68-1937.76) is a tight-range/bull-flag structure that resolved upward, consistent with trend continuation rather than a top.", "The latest leg (bars 114, 117) closes above both the 2680 range top and the 2771 prior swing high, so the current structure is a breakout to a new high, not a rotation inside the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Bar 120 holds above the 2680 range top and closes above its open (2686.59 versus 2684.16), so no bear breakout or acceptance back inside the range has occurred.", "The bearish bars after the high are small relative to the preceding bull bars (bar 119 range 145.44 versus bar 117 range 208.31), and no bear trend bar has follow-through."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars; window low 1368.42 (bar 10, open_time 1780704000000) and window high 2850 (bar 117, open_time 1789948800000); first close 2009.45 versus last close 2686.59.", "Bars 6-10 are five consecutive lower closes from 2006.17 to 1568.55, taking price to the window low 1368.42; bar 10 closes 1568.55 and leaves a 200.13-point lower tail (low 1368.42 versus close 1568.55).", "Bars 11-35 form a two-sided range with repeated highs at 1725.85 (bar 18) and 1845.09 (bar 19) and repeated lows at 1512.91 (bar 30) and 1551.60 (bar 34); bull and bear reversal bars alternate.", "Bars 36-49 rise on two wide bull trend bars (bar 36: 1608.68 to 1701.02; bar 48: 1775.60 to 1889.93, high 1891.66), reaching the 1944.39 high at bar 49.", "Bars 50-83 form a long, tight range: high 1974.46 (bar 61), low 1803.74 (bar 51); bars 73-83 overlap inside 1863.68-1937.76.", "Bar 84 (open_time 1787097600000) is a large bull trend bar, 1916.51 to 2252.16, closing 96% of its 377.29 range, the widest bar in the window, above the 1974.46 range top.", "Bars 87-113 hold a broad range: low 2357.18 (bar 98), high 2680 (bar 107); spike highs at 2557.46 (bar 92), 2680 (bar 107) and 2609.02 (bar 110) were each closed back inside the range.", "Bars 114-117 break upward: bar 114 closes 2612.02 (85% of its 206.65 range), bar 115 taps 2700, bar 117 reaches a new window high 2850 and closes 2775.61 with a 74.39-point upper tail.", "Bars 118-120 pull back: bar 119 is a bear bar closing 2684.16 in the lower quarter of its 145.44 range; bar 120 is a small bull bar (open 2684.16, close 2686.59) with low 2633.31, holding above the 2680 range top.", "Higher swing lows: 1368.42 (bar 10), 1512.91 (bar 30), 1597.72 (bar 36), 1803.74 (bar 51), 2357.18 (bar 98), 2633.31 (bar 120). Higher swing highs: 1944.39 (bar 49), 2771 (bar 86), 2850 (bar 117)."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Sell climax ending the window's down leg: bars 6-10 post five consecutive lower closes from 2006.17 to the window low 1368.42; bar 10 closes 1568.55 with a 200.13-point lower tail.", "end_time_ms": 1780703999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780358400000, "upper_boundary": "2006.17"}, {"description": "Post-sell-off two-sided range (bars 11-35): repeated tests of the 1512.91-1551.60 low area and the 1725.85-1845.09 high area, with most closes between 1550 and 1730.", "end_time_ms": 1782950399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Long, tight range (bars 50-83): high 1974.46 (bar 61), low 1803.74 (bar 51), compressing into 1863.68-1937.76 for bars 73-83 immediately before the bar 84 breakout.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "1803.74", "start_time_ms": 1784160000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull breakout and spike (bars 84-86): bar 84 runs 1916.51 to 2252.16 and closes near its high, above the 1974.46 range top; follow-through carries to the spike high 2771 at bar 86.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Broad post-spike range (bars 87-113): low 2357.18 (bar 98), high 2680 (bar 107); spike attempts at 2557.46, 2680 and 2609.02 all closed back inside.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Current bull leg (bars 114-117): two strong bull trend bars plus an overlapping pair break above the 2680 range top and the 2771 swing high to a new window high 2850; bars 118-120 pull back to 2633.31, still above 2680.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2850, or a bar closing in the upper third of its range above 2775.61, would confirm the breakout-spike read and favor trend continuation.", "Two consecutive closes below 2633.31 (bar 120 low) would indicate a failed breakout and rotation back into the 2357.18-2680 range, moving phase toward range.", "A strong bear trend bar closing below 2357.18 (bar 98 low) would end the sequence of higher swing lows and shift the regime read to trading-range or transition-unclear.", "Continued overlapping bars and closes inside 2633.31-2786.81 without reaching 2850 again would raise the odds that the last leg is a channel within a broad top, changing phase to channel and lowering always-in relevance.", "A pullback that holds above the 2436.87-2514.13 breakout area and then produces a close above 2786.81 would keep the bull-trend read while confirming the pullback as a buy-the-close-style continuation leg of the channel."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": "unclear", "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790323199999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The 2850 high (bar 97) is a spike with a long upper tail followed by 22 bars without a new high; highs step down to 2727.77 while the lows are two-sided, so the current state is a trading range and 'bull-trend' may be a holdover from earlier in the window.", "Bar 115's lower low (2633.31 vs 2648.49 at bar 110) breaks the immediate higher-low sequence inside the pullback, a first sign of weakening bull structure.", "The last four bars have small bodies and heavy overlap with no follow-through, which weakens evidence for trend continuation."], "evidence_for": ["Higher major swing lows 2358.62 (bar 63) -> 2568.16 (bar 91) -> 2633.31 (bar 115) keep the window's bull sequence intact at the swing scale.", "Two wide bull trend bars (bars 38 and 97) with closes well above their opens show strong bull initiative and follow-through into 2850.", "Window closes 2671.19, above the window open 2456.52 and above the 2568.16 higher low; the pullback from 2850 has not broken the prior major higher low."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens 2456.52 (bar 1) and closes 2671.19 (bar 120), +8.7%; window low 2358.62 (bar 63), window high 2850 (bar 97).", "Two wide bull trend bars anchor the advance: bar 38 (high 2680, low 2444.19, close 2555.52) and bar 97 (high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15), each closing in the upper half of its range.", "Bar 97 closes 126.85 below its 2850 high (long upper tail); subsequent highs step down: 2795 (bar 98), 2804.59 (bar 100), 2786.81 (bar 108), 2727.77 (bar 110).", "Major swing lows rise across the window: 2358.62 (bar 63) -> 2568.16 (bar 91) -> 2633.31 (bar 115).", "Bar 115 low 2633.31 undercuts bar 110 low 2648.49 by 15.18, then bar 116 closes 2682.25 (bull reversal bar off the low).", "Bars 117-120 overlap heavily (highs 2699.39/2695.78/2699.53/2683.74; lows 2660.49/2676.02/2673.88/2667.22) with small bodies of 11.84/7.50/9.07/6.09.", "The 2700 area was rejected intraday at bars 85 and 95 (both highs 2700) before the 2850 spike; the 2699.53 high (bar 119) restates that resistance."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Spike-and-channel bull leg from the bar-63 low 2358.62 to the bar-97 high 2850: a first spike around bar 80 (close 2578.60) and a second spike at bar 97 (close 2723.15), separated by shallow pullbacks with rising swing lows 2358.62 -> 2568.16.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Two-sided trading range since the 2850 spike: highs stopped at 2795 (bar 98), 2804.59 (bar 100) and lower, lows reached 2648.49 (bar 110) and 2633.31 (bar 115); price remains inside this band, roughly 7% below the 2850 high.", "end_time_ms": 1790323199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Bar 97 is a spike bar (high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) with a ~126.85-point upper tail and the largest range of the window; a candidate buy-climax/exhaustion bar, not a confirmed reversal.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Tight four-bar cluster (bars 117-120) with overlapping bodies and no directional follow-through, nested in the upper half of the pullback range near 2700 resistance.", "end_time_ms": 1790323199999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2660.49", "start_time_ms": 1790265600000, "upper_boundary": "2699.53"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull resumption: a trend bar closing above 2699.53 (bar 119 high) and then acceptance above 2804.59 (bar 100 high) with a following bar in the same direction.", "Range-to-bear transition: closes below 2633.31 (bar 115 low) and then below 2568.16 (bar 91 low) would break the sequence of higher swing lows.", "Breakout resolution of the tight 2660.49-2699.53 cluster (bars 117-120) by a trend bar closing beyond it with follow-through, which would define the next directional push."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2578.84", "close_time_ms": 1789898399999, "high": "2585.2", "low": "2572.71", "open": "2573.64", "open_time_ms": 1789894800000, "volume": "1191467.407"}, {"close": "2570.15", "close_time_ms": 1789901999999, "high": "2580", "low": "2569.99", "open": "2578.84", "open_time_ms": 1789898400000, "volume": "1087812.322"}, {"close": "2577.88", "close_time_ms": 1789905599999, "high": "2579.47", "low": "2568.16", "open": "2569.99", "open_time_ms": 1789902000000, "volume": "1630411.864"}, {"close": "2577.15", "close_time_ms": 1789909199999, "high": "2580.2", "low": "2571.48", "open": "2577.69", "open_time_ms": 1789905600000, "volume": "1550366.873"}, {"close": "2578.98", "close_time_ms": 1789912799999, "high": "2583.97", "low": "2575.72", "open": "2577.21", "open_time_ms": 1789909200000, "volume": "1425172.376"}, {"close": "2586", "close_time_ms": 1789916399999, "high": "2586", "low": "2574.59", "open": "2578.98", "open_time_ms": 1789912800000, "volume": "1932901.412"}, {"close": "2611", "close_time_ms": 1789919999999, "high": "2611", "low": "2584.37", "open": "2584.38", "open_time_ms": 1789916400000, "volume": "2203059.228"}, {"close": "2635.82", "close_time_ms": 1789923599999, "high": "2643.7", "low": "2605.96", "open": "2611", "open_time_ms": 1789920000000, "volume": "2239809.814"}, {"close": "2630.17", "close_time_ms": 1789927199999, "high": "2645.88", "low": "2624.89", "open": "2637.1", "open_time_ms": 1789923600000, "volume": "1845622.61"}, {"close": "2625.53", "close_time_ms": 1789930799999, "high": "2636.43", "low": "2622.06", "open": "2626.07", "open_time_ms": 1789927200000, "volume": "1973810.245"}, {"close": "2631.93", "close_time_ms": 1789934399999, "high": "2637.4", "low": "2624.63", "open": "2629.88", "open_time_ms": 1789930800000, "volume": "1523842.903"}, {"close": "2632.99", "close_ti